138
00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:11.890
Oh, yeah.

139
00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:12.930
I didn't even think about that.

140
00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:13.550
When we named Billy Merchant.

141
00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:13.710
Yeah.

142
00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:14.930
I feel like that's true.

143
00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:16.690
I got to talk to Marcus yesterday.

144
00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:19.030
Marcus, thanks so much for taking time out of your day.

145
00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:21.150
And here are a few things he shared with me.

146
00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:21.610
Okay.

147
00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:23.870
So he auditioned for Allison, Mindy, and Greg.

148
00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.370
And he said it went really, really well.

149
00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:26.330
He was really excited.

150
00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:29.250
You know that moment where you have a great meeting or a great audition?

151
00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:29.450
Yeah.

152
00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:30.410
He said that's how it felt.

153
00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:33.330
He had been in LA as a working actor for a while.

154
00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:37.250
And he said, this is one that I was like, ooh, ooh, I think I got it.

155
00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:40.250
And he said that Greg jumped up and shook his hand.

156
00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:40.790
Oh.

157
00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:41.970
And he was like, okay.

158
00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.630
And then he was running errands.

159
00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:44.770
He was at Home Depot.

160
00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:47.690
And he got the call that he got it.

161
00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.170
And his agent was like, you got it.

162
00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:50.870
And he was like, wait a second.

163
00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:51.610
I'm in Home Depot.

164
00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:52.670
I have to call you back.

165
00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:54.870
So he said he'll always remember that.

166
00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:59.650
And then he said the night before he had to come in, he was nervous.

167
00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:01.210
And he got like, no sleep.

168
00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:02.610
He said, I got zero sleep.

169
00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:07.090
He said, so then the next day I was freaking out because I hadn't gotten any sleep.

170
00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:10.310
And you know, it's like hard to remember your lines or anything.

171
00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:13.190
So he was like, I was really trying to wing it.

172
00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:15.210
And I said, well, we couldn't tell at all.

173
00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:17.270
Like, you were just such a cool customer.

174
00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:18.070
You had your lines.

175
00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.370
You were like totally ready to go.

176
00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:22.490
He said, Ange, I was like going on no sleep.

177
00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:23.090
Oh, my God.

178
00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:25.350
That happens to me always before a shoot.

179
00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:27.190
Yeah, or a big day, right?

180
00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:29.410
Like, whenever I have a big day, it's hard to sleep.

181
00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:33.150
